    "note": "Mratinje Dam's 220 m double-curvature arch, three crest spillways, five recessed hydraulic outlets, crown road, stepped gallery, two tunnel portals, photographed retaining grid and mapped service house on the fitted Piva gorge. The signed sea-level origin is 651 m, with the roadway at 678 m and foundation at 458 m. The fitted gorge uses the original standard terrain at its rim. Piva Lake renders at 651.65 m and the downstream reach at 534.18 m. The west road bench aligns the M-3 approach through the first cut in the limestone and transitions into the retained road at the retained PMTiles centerline. Only the mapped crest and connected grade inside the approach are replaced."
